Negative control for the resolved seam (T1.5 · S13 · AC8.5).

`ESC6` route (a) armed the seam, so `corpus-source.spec.ts`'s resolved branch is
now the live guard on provenance: what the seam hands a consumer must BE the
committed recording, not something shaped like one. This mutant swaps a single
recorded body for a hand-authored envelope built around the recording's own
rows — same addresses, same flags, same status, same row count.

What must go red is PROVENANCE, not the rows: the recording carries `version`,
`captured_at`, `brand_domain`, `source`, `provenance` and its response headers
beside `request`/`response`, and under the mutant that whole envelope is gone
because the served object was constructed here rather than read. An assertion
that only counts rows, reads `body.data`, or checks the ten keys are present
passes the mutant and proves nothing — the FE-2824 data-provenance shape. Only a
comparison of the served body against the committed file catches it.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

